      "description": "Watch Banfield vs Sarmiento Junin highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 29, 2026. The Liga Profesional Argentina encounter between Banfield and Sarmiento Junin promised a tactical battle as both sides looked to secure vital points. The match began with a high-intensity struggle in midfield, with neither team willing to give an inch in the opening exchanges. A Cagey Opening Half Played on July 29, 2026 , the first half was a testament to organized defending. Banfield attempted to build from the back, but Sarmiento 's discipline prevented any clear-cut opportunities. The referee brought a quiet first period to a close after three minutes of stoppage time, leaving the fans in anticipation of a breakthrough that seemed destined to come in the second act. Perrotta Ignites the Contest The second half saw an immediate shift in momentum. While Banfield introduced Bruno Sepulveda and Jhon Renteria at the break, it was Sarmiento who found their clinical edge. In the 53rd minute, David Zalazar turned provider for Tiziano Perrotta , who clinicaly finished to break the deadlock. The visitor's dominance was further underlined just six minutes later when Tomas Adoryan teed up Tiziano Perrotta for his second goal of the match, doubling the lead and stunning the home crowd. Late Drama and Clinical Finishing As the clock ticked down, the game erupted into a frenzy of goals. Banfield earned a lifeline in the 82nd minute when Bruno Sepulveda converted a penalty, but the joy was short-lived. Just two minutes later, Jonathan Herrera silenced the stadium by restoring the two-goal cushion. With Banfield pushed forward in desperation, Sarmiento struck again in the 86th minute through Junior Marabel , completing a devastating second-half performance that secured all three points for the visitors."
